    {
      "page_title": "Recovery with Reflog and rerere",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What is the reflog?",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==git reflog== lists where HEAD and branches pointed over time",
            "Works even after a rebase rewrote the history",
            "`git reflog show feature` shows one branch's history",
            "**Local only**: never pushed, never shared"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git reflog",
            "# HEAD@{0}: rebase (finish):",
            "#   returning to refs/heads/feature",
            "# HEAD@{3}: commit: add login"
          ],
          "note": "HEAD@{0} is always the newest entry"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. How long is it kept?",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Entry type",
            "Kept for"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Reachable",
              "~90 days"
            ],
            [
              "Unreachable",
              "~30 days"
            ],
            [
              "After gc",
              "Gone"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Why recovery works",
          "text": "Rebase makes NEW commits; the old ones stay in the object store until gc."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Undo a bad rebase",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git reset --hard ORIG_HEAD",
            "# or pick an exact entry:",
            "git reflog",
            "git reset --hard HEAD@{5}"
          ],
          "note": "--hard discards uncommitted work"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Run `git reflog`, find the line before the rebase",
            "Reset to `ORIG_HEAD` or that `HEAD@{n}`",
            "Check `git log` matches your old history"
          ],
          "style": "number"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Rescue a dropped commit",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git reflog          # find a1b2c3d",
            "git branch rescue a1b2c3d",
            "git log rescue     # verify"
          ],
          "note": "Pin it before gc collects it"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A commit dropped in `rebase -i` is not gone: grab its ==SHA== from the reflog and pin it with a branch."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. rerere: reuse recorded resolution",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Git **remembers** how you resolved a conflict",
            "Next identical conflict is auto-resolved from `.git/rr-cache`",
            "You still `git add` and `git rebase --continue`",
            "Great for long-lived branches rebased repeatedly"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git config rerere.enabled true",
            "git rerere forget src/app.js"
          ],
          "note": "forget clears a wrong resolution"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Expecting teammates' reflog to help you: it is **local**",
            "Waiting past ~30 days, then hunting for the SHA",
            "Trusting a bad rerere result: use `forget`, redo it",
            "Running `reset --hard` with uncommitted edits"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "git",
      "subtitle": "Undo and remember"
