      "page_title": "Rebase Mistakes: Shared History & Mid-Rebase",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Mistakes: Shared History",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Rebasing a public branch like `main` or a shared `develop`",
            "Plain `--force` instead of ==--force-with-lease==",
            "Rebase rewrites SHAs, so refs in issues and notes go **stale**",
            "Giant 50-commit rebase: squash first, or rebase in smaller steps"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git push --force # blind",
            "git push --force-with-lease # safe",
            "git rebase -i HEAD~50 # too big",
            "git rebase -i HEAD~8 # smaller"
          ],
          "note": "lease fails if remote moved"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Mistakes: Mid-Rebase",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Running `git commit` in a conflict instead of `--continue`",
            "Confusing ours and theirs, keeping the **wrong** side",
            "Aborting after resolving: the finished work is gone",
            "No tests after rebase; a clean replay can still break behavior"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Word",
            "During rebase",
            "Holds"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "ours",
              "the new base",
              "upstream commits"
            ],
            [
              "theirs",
              "commit being replayed",
              "YOUR change"
            ],
            [
              "trap",
              "looks reversed",
              "vs merge"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Lost work after abort?",
          "text": "`git reflog`, then `git reset --hard HEAD@{n}` brings it back."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Safety Habits",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git branch backup-feature",
            "git rebase --autostash main",
            "git pull --rebase",
            "npm test # verify the replay"
