            "Reordering lines can cause conflicts",
            "Empty todo **aborts** the rebase",
            "`exec npm test` checks after a commit"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Golden rule",
          "text": "Rewrite only commits **nobody else has**. Pushed and pulled by others? Merge instead."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. ☆ Merge Flavors",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==Fast-forward==: target has no new commits, pointer just moves",
            "`--no-ff` forces a merge commit with two parents",
            "Rebase first, then fast-forward for a **linear** history",
            "Merge is non-destructive; rebase rewrites history"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git switch feature",
            "git rebase main",
            "git switch main",
            "git merge --no-ff feature"
          ],
          "note": "no-ff keeps the branch visible"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. ☆ How Replay Works",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Find the **merge-base** of branch and upstream",
            "Collect commits in `upstream..HEAD`",
            "Detach HEAD and checkout the upstream tip",
            "Cherry-pick each commit in order",
            "Move the branch name to the last new commit"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Tip",
          "text": "Commits whose patch-id is already upstream are skipped automatically."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. ☆ Moving with --onto",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Argument",
            "Answers"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`<newbase>`",
              "where to land"
            ],
            [
              "`<oldbase>`",
              "where to cut"
            ],
            [
              "`<branch>`",
              "what to move"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git rebase --onto main \\",
            "  feature topic",
            "git log --graph --oneline --all"
          ],
          "note": "only topic moves; feature stays"
        },
